WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.250
Will the Last Man on Earth

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:06.090
escape the TV scifi comedy curse?

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:07.090
I have the answer--

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:08.500
--on this week's episode

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.230
of Angry Nerd!

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:11.350
First, your comments.

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:12.570
AT Jamin writes,

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:13.570
“Can you talk about”

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:14.570
“Netflix's upcoming”

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:15.570
“Legend of Zelda show?”

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:16.570
Hey, alls I know

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:18.039
for sure about it

00:00:18.039 --> 00:00:19.039
is that it's

00:00:19.039 --> 00:00:20.039
going to be better

00:00:20.039 --> 00:00:26.980
than the Zelda CD-i game.

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:28.510
What was up with that?

00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:30.020
How was THAT a thing?

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:31.310
So Will Forte's new series

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:32.310
Last Man on Earth

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:33.430
is like a funny take

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:34.610
on I Am Legend...

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:35.610
but with no

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:36.610
vampire zombies.

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:37.610
Now, I'm a sucker

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:38.610
for the “Man Alone”

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:39.789
subgenre of scifi,

00:00:39.789 --> 00:00:40.789
because it can be

00:00:40.789 --> 00:00:41.969
bleak AND funny

00:00:41.969 --> 00:00:43.059
at the same time.

00:00:43.059 --> 00:00:44.059
Like Charlton Heston

00:00:44.059 --> 00:00:45.059
in Omega Man

00:00:45.059 --> 00:00:46.059
lipsynching along

00:00:46.059 --> 00:00:52.940
with a movie he's seen a hundred times.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:54.069
Or when Bruno Lawrence

00:00:54.069 --> 00:00:55.170
cracks up and

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:57.549
declares himself planetary president

00:00:57.549 --> 00:01:08.250
in The Quiet Earth.

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:09.250
Or that episode of

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:10.250
Twilight Zone where

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:11.250
Burgess Meredith

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:12.250
is finally alone

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:13.250
with all of the books

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:15.100
that he's eager to read...

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:16.759
and he breaks his glasses.

00:01:16.759 --> 00:01:18.570
“THAT’S NOT FAIR…”

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:21.579
“THAT’S NOT FAIR AT ALL!”

00:01:21.579 --> 00:01:22.579
Ugh, that scene

00:01:22.579 --> 00:01:23.579
always makes me want

00:01:23.579 --> 00:01:24.649
to duct tape my glasses

00:01:24.649 --> 00:01:25.680
to my noggin.

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:27.810
Anyway, I really like the dry,

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:29.079
laughtrack-free humor of

00:01:29.079 --> 00:01:30.399
Last Man on Earth!

00:01:30.399 --> 00:01:31.560
You can tell it was produced by

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:33.729
the genius comedy team Lord and Miller,

00:01:33.729 --> 00:01:34.970
who made 21 Jump Street

00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:36.280
and the Lego Movie.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:37.280
BY THE WAY,

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:38.280
HOW EFFED UP IS IT

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:39.280
THAT LEGO MOVIE

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:41.650
DIDN'T GET AN OSCAR NOM?!

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:42.650
Last Man on Earth

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:43.650
is also a nice change of pace

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:46.590
from most American scifi comedy series.

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:47.590
Think about it--

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:48.670
the biggest hits are always

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:49.670
the broadest,

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:50.670
silliest,

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:53.420
lowest common denominator-iest stuff!

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:54.420
Alf,

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:55.420
My Favorite Martian,

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:56.420
Mork &amp; Mindy,

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:57.420
Third Rock from the Sun...

00:01:57.420 --> 00:01:58.460
I mean, none of them

00:01:58.460 --> 00:01:59.460
are that different

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:00.600
from a Family Matters episode

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:02.409
where Urkel makes a bizarre contraption.

00:02:02.409 --> 00:02:04.170
The Brits have a much higher class

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:05.170
of scifi comedy--

00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:06.640
I think it's partly the influence

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:08.479
of Doctor Who, which could never

00:02:08.479 --> 00:02:10.830
really take itself TOO seriously

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:13.600
because the effects were so laughable.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:14.600
The UK gave us

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.160
Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:18.520
by Doctor Who alum Douglas Adams,

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:20.060
Red Dwarf,

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:21.060
Hyperdrive,

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:22.390
2point4 Children,

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:23.670
Goodnight Sweetheart,

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:25.360
No Heroics…

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.250
All worth seeking out.

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:28.250
All light years

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:29.530
beyond Alf.

00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:30.860
The closest we get to

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:32.760
gut-busting science fiction on TV

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:33.760
in America

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:36.640
are SyFy channel monster movies.

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:38.280
I don’t care what you say--

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:39.860
Sharknado is overrated!

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:40.870
it's all about

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:42.690
MegaShark versus Crocasaurus.

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:43.690
Mwah!

00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:45.320
But I demand to see

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:47.310
more American TV scifi

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:49.680
that is hilarious ON PURPOSE!

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:50.700
Annnnnnd...cut!

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:53.530
So was that last take okay?

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:55.960
Do I need to redo it?

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:58.630
Hey, where'd everyone go?

00:02:58.630 --> 00:02:59.820
Hello?

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:01.010
Helloooo?

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:04.590
They're all gone!

00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:06.320
I'm the last man on Earth!

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:08.020
Oh, at last!

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:09.200
I finally have the time

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:11.320
to read my backlog of comics

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:12.840
with no interruptions!

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:14.160
I can finally--

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.350
can finally--

00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:18.550
Not fair!

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:21.840
It's not fair!

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:23.920
IT'S NOT FAIR!!!!

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:26.750
Hey, I don’t care if

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:28.190
the Korean taco truck is going by--

00:03:28.190 --> 00:03:30.440
don’t leave me alone on this set again!

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:31.440
What do you think of

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:32.440
Last Man on Earth?

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:33.570
And what's your favorite

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:35.310
scifi comedy series,

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:36.310
American or otherwise?

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:37.590
Let me know in the comments,

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:39.050
subscribe to the Wired channel,

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:40.570
and click on these other videos

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:42.090
to watch more of my rants!

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:43.540
If you don't click,

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:44.720
those other versions of me

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:46.400
will just be stuck sitting there--

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:47.980
alone!

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:49.570
Cut off from humanity!

00:03:49.570 --> 00:03:50.980
Gradually driven insane

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:54.010
by the oppressive solitude!

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:55.360
What?

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:59.020
You're STILL not clicking?!

00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:00.020
You heartless monster!

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:03.310
How can you live with yourself?

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:04.470
I'll bet your top 10

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:05.840
desert island DVDs

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:07.880
are all Michael Bay movies!

